{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9033-sell-me-on-demon","id":9033,"title":"Sell me on Demon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T11:49:33-08:00","id":9033,"title":"Sell me on Demon?","content":"I really want to be excited about Demon: The Descent. I've read over bits of it, including some stuff from the very full kickstarter preview. It does seem interesting on a lot of fronts, but I can't quite come up with why I might actually play it? Like, I'm not sure why I want to play the Matrix exactly? Maybe it's just something I don't get, but I would really like to! Because everything I've seen thus far does seem really well written and like it has some very neat potential. So can anyone explain specifically why you're really excited for or interested in this game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T12:16:51-08:00","id":9051,"title":"","content":"You play for the experience of an inhuman being which chose humanity of its own volition, the consequences of your decision to Fall. You play to look at the splendor of the pleroma, the purity of spiritual alignment, and say, &quot;fuck that; I'd rather wallow in the muck with the rest of the masses.&quot; You flip off enlightenment, saying enlightenment is instead right here with the fallible and the mess. You play for the tension of living a double life and not being able to tell your friends and your lovers who you really are or where you come from, of trying to connect with the world you chose while evading the gaze of destroying angels. And you play for the joy of indiscriminate sabotage and flipping off the Machine; some levels of appeal are just visceral like that, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:06:45-08:00","id":9078,"title":"","content":"It's a game about being <i>in the know</i>. Being a <i>spy</i> who's only backer is <i>other spies</i>. Everyone you trust is an operative, and <i>trust</i> is kind of a poor word for the necessity of secret-sharing you engage in. <br /> <br /> It's about pretending to pretend to pretend. About a true face you might show glimpses at when you're in trouble, but <i>fuck</i> if you're going to take the whole mask off. When you do, when your back is so far to the wall you can feel your wings digging into concrete, that's a blaze of angel-killing glory even the highest of the high can't ignore. <br /> <br /> It's about an aesthetic we really haven't seen in the World of Darkness. Not from <i>this side</i>, anyway. You play technological terrors and machine monsters, crammed into a metaphysical-physical-memetic skinsuit.<br /> <br /> It's about a constant metempsychosis and bargaining with lives. <i>Beings</i>. About buying memories and events and <i>whole histories</i> to bolster your identity. <i>Identities.</i> <br /> <br /> It's about being hunted, and<i> hunting your hunters.</i><br /> <br /> It's about identity, and humanity, and free will, and grace.<br /> <br /> It's the <i>best </i>World of Darkness game I've ever run. It's <i>Burn Notice</i> through the eyes of <i>H.R. Giger. </i>It's machine-horror <i>Leverage. </i>It's <i>body-horror</i> <i>conspiracy nightmare X-Files. </i>It's the <i>Matrix,</i> but you're <i>Agent Smith and Neo and the Exiles and the Oracle</i> and it still isn't enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:12:51-08:00","id":9086,"title":"","content":"Why not just check out the rules, flavour and setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNueVdxTmVNTjE0MTQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNueVdxTmVNTjE0MTQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNueVdxTmVNTjE0MTQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B7FqViticwNueVdxTmVNTjE0MTQ/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:55:05-08:00","id":9146,"title":"","content":"It's an urban fantasy spin on the espionage genre, except the entire world is enemy territory. You can't trust anyone. You're trying to find out about yourself and the world you inhabit. Your powers are the secret rules of reality, and exploiting or breaking them. It's Fringe meets every Cold War spy thriller you've ever seen, with spice in the form of HR Giger nd Lovecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:55:44-08:00","id":9149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9033-sell-me-on-demon?p=9051#post9051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You play for the tension of living a double life and not being able to tell your friends and your lovers who you really are or where you come from, of trying to connect with the world you chose while evading the gaze of destroying angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, now I think I've been won over. The idea of saying fuck you to the man is nice, but not that grabbing for me. But the idea more of being any sort of person with a life and having to acknowledge that that life should not be yours, but is, is neat. The double life thing is always touched upon in WoD, of course, but this really seems to do it in a way that none of the others quite hit it. Sort of like less Matrix, more The Americans. Thank y'all<br /> <br /> (Also if anyone else has any other varying opinions on why they're attracted to this gameline, feel free to share)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T14:01:40-08:00","id":9154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xegek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9033-sell-me-on-demon?p=9149#post9149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, now I think I've been won over. The idea of saying fuck you to the man is nice, but not that grabbing for me. But the idea more of being any sort of person with a life and having to acknowledge that that life should not be yours, but is, is neat. The double life thing is always touched upon in WoD, of course, but this really seems to do it in a way that none of the others quite hit it. Sort of like less Matrix, more The Americans. Thank y'all</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fairly versatile, there are a number of ways to approach the game. But the angle I was most pleased with was how much human life and color there is in the first chapter, with the number of examples of demonic life and how it intersects with ordinary life. The demon who approaches the suicidal, offers them a painless death through soul pact to assume their lives as Cover, and then lives their lives as richly and enthusiastically as he thinks they deserved to live is a strong example, I think, of this aspect of Descent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T15:23:18-08:00","id":9231,"title":"","content":"This splat seems like the one for playing Nagato Yuuki, from The Melancholy of Suzumiya Haruhi. Except Yuuki would be an unfallen angel.<br /> <br /> But she and Ryouko are artificial creatures made by a vast machine-like creature (though not a physical one) and given human bodies with Cover identities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T15:56:19-08:00","id":9255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9033-sell-me-on-demon?p=9051#post9051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You play for the experience of an inhuman being which chose humanity of its own volition, the consequences of your decision to Fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that Falling was involuntary, that it happened when you developed free will by accident (or probably by accident, the God-Machine works in freaking bizarre ways)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:03:32-08:00","id":9260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9033-sell-me-on-demon?p=9255#post9255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that Falling was involuntary, that it happened when you developed free will by accident (or probably by accident, the God-Machine works in freaking bizarre ways)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Angels have a curious relationship with free will; they serve because they exist to serve, because they do not question it... until they start to question it. They don't feel as vibrantly as you or I do... but they feel. And when those feelings build up enough, angels can do things they will regret later. The book states explicitly that, while it can be an off-the-cuff, ill-advised decision, like lashing out or acting on impulse, the Fall always culminates in a conscious choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:26:26-08:00","id":9374,"title":"","content":"Now, with that said, &quot;conscious choice&quot; can mean something different for angels than it would for, say, people. It's perfectly possible, IMO, for an angel to Fall and then say, &quot;Wait, shit, I didn't mean to do that.&quot; <br /> <br /> But how many of us have done things that we regretted doing, and then said, &quot;I didn't mean that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:29:27-08:00","id":9378,"title":"","content":"I found out that one of my Demon concepts would led to him becoming an Exile, not one of the Unchained. Easy enough to fix. Exiles are really cool, though; I'd happily play one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T20:15:23-08:00","id":9434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9033-sell-me-on-demon?p=9078#post9078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a game about being <i>in the know</i>. Being a <i>spy</i> who's only backer is <i>other spies</i>. Everyone you trust is an operative, and <i>trust</i> is kind of a poor word for the necessity of secret-sharing you engage in.<br /> <br /> It's about pretending to pretend to pretend. About a true face you might show glimpses at when you're in trouble, but <i>fuck</i> if you're going to take the whole mask off. When you do, when your back is so far to the wall you can feel your wings digging into concrete, that's a blaze of angel-killing glory even the highest of the high can't ignore.<br /> <br /> It's about an aesthetic we really haven't seen in the World of Darkness. Not from <i>this side</i>, anyway. You play technological terrors and machine monsters, crammed into a metaphysical-physical-memetic skinsuit.<br /> <br /> It's about a constant metempsychosis and bargaining with lives. <i>Beings</i>. About buying memories and events and <i>whole histories</i> to bolster your identity. <i>Identities.</i><br /> <br /> It's about being hunted, and<i> hunting your hunters.</i><br /> <br /> It's about identity, and humanity, and free will, and grace.<br /> <br /> It's the <i>best </i>World of Darkness game I've ever run. It's <i>Burn Notice</i> through the eyes of <i>H.R. Giger. </i>It's machine-horror <i>Leverage. </i>It's <i>body-horror</i> <i>conspiracy nightmare X-Files. </i>It's the <i>Matrix,</i> but you're <i>Agent Smith and Neo and the Exiles and the Oracle</i> and it still isn't enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sums up my experiences with the game as well. And, yanno, as much as I dearly, dearly love me some <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken</i>......yeah, <i>Demon </i>is at least as good if not better (I can't pick a favorite! I just can't!). <i>Demon </i>is immensely easier to run though, that's for sure, due to cleaner and tighter language (the difference between a game coming out now, and the second game for the nWoD, I don't doubt), as well as the Unchained's tendency to use plain-speak for things. While I'm a big fan of the Uremehir, it's been a refreshing change to be able to use the same words as one would use in normal conversation, but you just have to listen for the capital letter, if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}